<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Captaincy General of the Philippines</h1><p class="st-meta">1565 CE – 1898 CE · capital Manila (Cebu until 1571)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Spain's colony in the Philippines from 1565 to 1898, governed from Manila and linked to the Americas by the Manila galleon.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi">Miguel Lopez de Legazpi</a> arrived from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-spain">New Spain</a> in 1565, founded a settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cebu">Cebu</a> and in 1571 took the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-maynila">Kingdom of Maynila</a>, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> the capital. The islands, named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II</a>, were administered through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">Viceroyalty of New Spain</a> until Mexican independence in 1821.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A governor-general ruled with the Real <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audiencia">Audiencia</a>, while friars of the religious orders converted most lowland Filipinos to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> and wielded great local power. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila-galleon">Manila galleons</a> carried Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acapulco">Acapulco</a> for Mexican <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> from 1565 to 1815. Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-basco-y-vargas">Jose Basco y Vargas</a> introduced the tobacco monopoly in 1782. Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a> and Sulu resisted conquest.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in 1762 to 1764. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nationalism">Nationalism</a> grew after the Cavite mutiny of 1872, and the execution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-rizal">Jose Rizal</a> in 1896 fed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution">Philippine Revolution</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ceded the islands to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1898">Treaty of Paris</a> of 1898.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/captaincy-general-of-the-philippines.jpg" alt="Captaincy General of the Philippines" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: previous version User:Ignaciogavira ; current version HansenBCN, designs from SanchoPanzaXXI · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Spain_(1785%E2%80%931873,_1875%E2%80%931931).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1565 CE – 1898 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Manila (Cebu until 1571)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Miguel Lopez de Legazpi, Jose Basco y Vargas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, Tagalog, Cebuano</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/philippines">Philippines</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Spanish Philippines, Spanish East Indies, Philippine Islands (Spanish)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1732&amp;focus=captaincy-general-of-the-philippines" aria-label="Captaincy General of the Philippines on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7989 1634 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Captaincy General of the Philippines lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8309 1890L8544 2411M8309 1890L8467 2099M8309 1890L8308 189